tration, and securities lending services. The company was founded in 1873 and is headquartered in Chiyoda, Japan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Masahiro  Kihara | President, Group CEO, Representative Corporate Executive & Executive Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $999,034 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 52K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Mizuho Financial Group, Inc. Sp is a large-cap financial services business with a $124.8B market cap on $58.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +23% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $13.9B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 56% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5637752327679438},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Marriott International (NASDAQ:MAR) Stock: Insider Benjamin Breland Sells 2,408 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/marriott-international-nasdaqmar-stock-insider-benjamin-breland-sells-2408-shares.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794609944.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.91,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Deal Behind Mizuho\u2019s Downgrade of Surgery Partners (SGRY)","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/deal-behind-mizuho-downgrade-surgery-211048170.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794604248.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.637,"tier":2,"scope"